From fccc9cab60e7dcd068f0431a6dbe4ec4e4c46fa6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joel Brower <joel.brower@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 07:20:03 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] feat(android): build an installable APK without Gradle or
 the NDK

Process mode: the Go core is built as a pure android/arm64 executable, which
needs no cgo and so no NDK, ships as a native library, and runs as a child
process reached over a loopback port with a per-launch token. It exits with
the app. Core.java picks JNI or process mode at startup; nothing above it
changes. The app no longer depends on AndroidX, so android/build-apk.sh can
assemble it with aapt, javac, dx, zipalign and apksigner alone.

Also: pass the phone's time zone to the core, which otherwise runs on UTC
(alarms, clock sync), and correct the note on Wi-Fi binding, which reaches
the WebView but not Go's raw sockets.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016wzfhQtsFu3EKKkUkehQyh
